  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A horizontal overhead powerline is at height of $4 \\mathrm{~m}$ from the ground and carries a current of $100 \\mathrm{~A}$ from east to west. The magnetic field directly below it on the ground is $\\left(\\mu_{0}=4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{Tm} \\mathrm{A}^{-1}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qVMgA",
      "text": "$2.5 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~T}$ southward",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AoNlf",
      "text": "$5 \\times 10^{-6}$ T northward",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "taPpd",
      "text": "$5 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~T}$ southward",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xrFPf",
      "text": "$2.5 \\times 10^{-7}$ T northward",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The magnetic field is\r\n$\\mathrm{B}=\\frac{\\mu_{0}}{4 \\pi} \\frac{2 \\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{r}}=10^{-7} \\times \\frac{2 \\times 100}{4}=5 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~T}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/fXNqXasjtRkq7PU3M79o92MfBcmfgd2vd8nB1h7sNF4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\nAccording to right hand palm rule, the magnetic field is directed towards south.",
    "image": null
  },
